eal estate industry leader in sustainability, with 100% of our in-service office buildings LEED certified and over 95% certified LEED Gold or Platinum. Vornado Realty Trust was incorporated in 1946 in Maryland, USA.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven  Roth | Chairman of the Board & CEO | Age 83 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $576K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers. Each employee generates $306K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Vornado Realty Trust is a mid-cap real estate business with a $7.2B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are expanding by +2.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $962M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 53 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 7.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 3.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 1850% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2242004.0},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 50% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 45% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Real Estate peers","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Vornado Realty Trust (VNO) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/How_Vornado_Realty_Trust_VNO_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_112426035401_1